Version 1.30 (2012/11/02)

Common:
- example of use (window$ only).

rrenc, rrdec:
- port to Linux added.

m2cdm:
- preserve original timestamps of files placed on disc;
- some compiler warnings fixed;
- use compilation date instead of predefined one.

Version 1.29 (2006/02/27)
Lightweight (rr-1.29.update) package.

Common:
- cdrtfe (cdrtools & mode2cdmaker front-end) by Oliver Valencia
  (http://home.arcor.de/kerberos002/) now supports error protection
  of XCD discs;
- fixed bug in m2cdm paramfile composer;
- GUI front-end integration is improved (status line output).

Version 1.28 (2006/02/24)
Lightweight (rr-1.28.update) package.

Common:
- fixed bug in command-line parser.

Version 1.27 (2006/02/20)
Lightweight (rr-1.27.update) package (main files only); designed to use
together with rr-1.24.extra package.

Common:
- max linesize of .rrt file increased up to ~1080 bytes (for long
  comments, especially rrenc's command-line copy);
- fixed bug in comment processing module (crash if buffer overflows);
- new RR-list option added: -e <ext> - custom extension of XCD files;
- GUI front-end integration is slightly improved.

Version 1.26 (2006/02/15)
Lightweight (rr-1.26.update) package (main files only); designed to use
together with rr-1.24.extra package.

Common:
- fixed few bugs in support of absolute paths.

rrenc:
- new command-line option added: --keep-old-ext (as m2cdm -extname).

rrdec:
- fixed serious bug in 1.25 which might cause mixing of directories;
- support for XDC-discs made with -extname option.

Version 1.25 (2006/02/13)
Lightweight (rr-1.25.update) package (main files only); designed to use
together with rr-1.24.extra package.

Common:
- the project has its own site - http://elicit.vn.ua/;
- few small bugs fixed.

rrenc:
- support for absolute paths added (in --process-dir mode only)
  in source filelist (when --source-dir is empty) and in destination
  files (when --target-dir is empty);
- new command-line option added: --multi-track
- new RR-list option added: -u
- output of command-line into RR-list added;
- built-in help improved and slightly reordered, info about errorlevels
  added.

rrdec:
- new RR-list option added: -u
- built-in help improved and slightly reordered.

Version 1.24 (2006/01/30)
Split into two package:
- rr-1.24.main - exe's and minimum set of texts; main goal is smallest
  package size;
- rr-1.24.extra - extended set of docs and other auxiliary files.

Common:
- few small bugs fixed.

Version 1.23 (2005/06/23) (internal release)
Lightweight (update) package (.exe files only); designed to replace programs
in package of version 1.20.

Common:
- updated: max redundancy sector count is increased up to 60000.

Version 1.22 (2005/06/01) (internal release)
Lightweight (update) package (.exe files only); designed to replace programs
in package of version 1.20.

Common:
- fixed: error in processing of zero-length files.

Version 1.21 (2005/05/25)
Lightweight (update) package (.exe files only); designed to replace programs
in package of version 1.20.

Common:
- fixed: error in polynom-computing library (abnormal temination on
  non-Intel processors).

rrenc:
- fixed: error in "--process-dir" switch processing.

Version 1.20 (2005/05/18)

Common:
- m2cdm-paramfile creation algorythm is slightly improved;
- added support of Russian letters in filenames;
- m2cdm-paramfile's "-isolevel1" now autoswitches off if there are filenames
  not compatible with ISO Level 1 (i.e. 8.3 and [A-Z0-9_]);
- Russian documentation is made, tranlation into English already started.

rrenc:
- added switch "--process-dir", concerning to "-d <dir>" lines in source
  filelist;
- added switch "--ansi-charset" - assumes source filelist and generated
  .rrt file must be encoded in ANSI (otherwise OEM assumes - important for
  Russian letters in filenames);
- "--target-dir" switch processing fixed (.rrt file was created in wrong
  directory).

rrdec:
- "--keep-broken" switch processing fixed (some underrecovered files was
  marked as totally recovered);
- added "-a" directive for .rrt file meaning that file is encoded in ANSI
  (otherwise OEM assumes - important for Russian letters in filenames).

m2cdm:
- fixed support for Russian letters in filenames in case if no "-isolevel1" /
  "-isolevel2" parameter;
- fixed support for OEM/ANSI codepage switch;
- files/parameters in command line is not allowed now (except "-paramfile"
  parameter); all parameters is passed thru paramfile.  

Version 1.19 (2005/04/10)

Changelog is lost :-(
